    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="8" relname="span">I believe intuitiveness with regards to HCI can be defined as how quickly or how easily one can grasp a particular concept.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="10" relname="circumstance">When it comes to an interface being intuitive</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="10" relname="span">I think that it depends on a person experiences, and cultural differences.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="11" relname="span">The more familiar a person is with a concept the more intuitive an interface can be.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="6" relname="concession">Companies such as Microsoft ATTEMPT to make their products intuitive,</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="13" relname="span">but I believe that if someone is unfamiliar with a word processor for example, Microsoft Word would be a learning experience for them</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="13" relname="antithesis">rather than something that is intuitive to them.</segment>
        <group id="8" type="span"/>
        <group id="9" type="span" parent="1" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="9" relname="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="3" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="4" relname="evidence"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="12" relname="span"/>
    </body>
</rst>
